WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.200
- Because I feel like you
have some kind of spidey sense

00:00:02.200 --> 00:00:03.033
with singers.

00:00:03.033 --> 00:00:04.990
Like, you know, I've
seen him on many shows

00:00:04.990 --> 00:00:07.100
and I think there's something
about you, you can always

00:00:07.100 --> 00:00:07.933
kind of recognize it.

00:00:07.933 --> 00:00:09.760
Whether it's One
Direction, all those guys,

00:00:09.760 --> 00:00:11.730
or Camila Cabello, me, there's too many,

00:00:11.730 --> 00:00:13.270
I could name so many.

00:00:13.270 --> 00:00:14.730
But what do you,

00:00:14.730 --> 00:00:18.590
what do you think you catch
that maybe nobody else does?

00:00:18.590 --> 00:00:21.010
- For me, you can see it in people's eyes.

00:00:21.010 --> 00:00:21.843
You know?

00:00:21.843 --> 00:00:24.990
It's like, if you've got
that kind of, it's something

00:00:24.990 --> 00:00:28.580
when you look in someone's
eyes when they audition,

00:00:28.580 --> 00:00:30.330
you're like fearless.

00:00:30.330 --> 00:00:33.520
And even if it's not perfect,
this is just something

00:00:33.520 --> 00:00:34.430
you recognize.

00:00:34.430 --> 00:00:36.700
I wouldn't say I get it
right a hundred percent.

00:00:36.700 --> 00:00:38.750
But most times-
- You get it right a lot-

00:00:38.750 --> 00:00:41.310
- I've got a pretty good track
record and that's what I do.

00:00:41.310 --> 00:00:43.830
I look in someone's eyes
and I can see whether

00:00:43.830 --> 00:00:45.450
they're confident or not.

00:00:45.450 --> 00:00:49.390
And whether they've got great
taste is another part of it.

00:00:49.390 --> 00:00:50.730
Because a lot of time people come on

00:00:50.730 --> 00:00:52.500
with the wrong song choices.
- Song selection.

00:00:52.500 --> 00:00:54.010
- Why did you choose that song?

00:00:54.010 --> 00:00:56.700
Or why didn't you do
something creative with it?

00:00:56.700 --> 00:01:00.210
I mean, that's when I get
frustrated, but look, it's hard,

00:01:00.210 --> 00:01:04.060
but it's still the most
amazing feeling, you know?

00:01:04.060 --> 00:01:06.940
When you always remember
that audition, when

00:01:06.940 --> 00:01:09.920
you meet the star for the first
time and that's, you know,

00:01:09.920 --> 00:01:12.030
genuinely why I still do the job now.

00:01:12.030 --> 00:01:15.090
- That's gotta be so cool
too, that you see so young.

00:01:15.090 --> 00:01:16.640
Like I was 19, a lot of those

00:01:16.640 --> 00:01:18.010
like One Direction boys, they were really,

00:01:18.010 --> 00:01:18.843
they were younger than that.

00:01:18.843 --> 00:01:20.220
Like, and then you see them now

00:01:20.220 --> 00:01:21.690
and they all have their separate careers

00:01:21.690 --> 00:01:23.310
and they're all, that's just crazy.

00:01:23.310 --> 00:01:25.632
- Oh, amazing, and Camila was,

00:01:25.632 --> 00:01:27.590
she wasn't even meant to audition.

00:01:27.590 --> 00:01:30.110
She wasn't, I think we were like

00:01:30.110 --> 00:01:32.080
on time or something that particular day

00:01:32.080 --> 00:01:33.940
which meant when she was a reserve

00:01:33.940 --> 00:01:35.790
and I went backstage to have a cigarette

00:01:35.790 --> 00:01:38.614
and she was lying on the floor crying.

00:01:38.614 --> 00:01:40.220
I went what's the matter.

00:01:40.220 --> 00:01:41.840
She said they weren't let me audition.

00:01:41.840 --> 00:01:43.830
And I went, well, just go and audition.

00:01:43.830 --> 00:01:45.670
So she came out five minutes later.

00:01:45.670 --> 00:01:46.503
Amazing.

